## Context

The paper's §4 states citation coverage "approximately 27% before 2007
versus 47% post-2015" — v1.0 figures. On corpus v2 a quick recomputation
(share of DOI-bearing refined works appearing as citing source in
refined_citations) gives ~86% / ~77%: the GROBID and catalog-stage
reference layers lifted early-period coverage so much the gradient may
have inverted. A TODO comment marks the paragraph
(deliverables/data-paper/data-paper.qmd, §4 Descriptive statistics).

## Actions

